.TH FL-VIEW 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-view \- image viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-view\fR [\fIIMAGE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows images and lets you step through the
other images of the same folder with the arrow keys. +/\- zoom, 1 original size, F fit,
L/R rotate, H flip, F5 slideshow, F11 fullscreen, Delete moves to the trash.
.PP
Photos are shown upright as the camera recorded them (the EXIF orientation).
\fBI\fR shows the image information: the file, its size and dimensions, and for photos the
camera, lens, date, exposure, focal length, flash and the place where it was taken
(\fBShow on Map\fR opens it on OpenStreetMap).
.PP
A strip of thumbnails of the folder runs along the bottom; a click shows a picture, the
mouse wheel scrolls it and \fBT\fR hides or shows it.
.SS Editing
\fBC\fR crops: drag over the part to keep, then Enter (Escape cancels). Ctrl+R resizes, with
the proportions kept unless turned off. Rotating and flipping are edits too. Ctrl+S saves the
changed picture over the file (after asking), Ctrl+Shift+S saves it under another name, as PNG
or JPEG by the name's ending; leaving a changed picture asks first. Saving a JPEG does not
keep its camera information.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/view.ini\fR
\fB[View]\fR Thumbnails=true|false.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-session\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1)
